*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
orion.db*

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Cargo.lock for the app crate.
#
# Deliberately NOT committed. It was added by accident in the M1 merge, from a
# Linux sandbox build, and immediately collided with the lockfile on a
# contributor's Windows machine ("untracked working tree files would be
# overwritten by merge").
#
# The usual advice is to commit lockfiles for binaries, and that is right for
# reproducibility. It is not workable here yet: this crate is built on Linux,
# Windows and macOS by different people, and Tauri resolves some dependencies
# per platform. Revisit once CI pins the toolchain and generates the lockfile
# on one platform.
src-tauri/Cargo.lock

# Private research papers & enterprise presentations (untracked)
docs/*[pP][aA][pP][eE][rR]*
docs/*[pP][rR][eE][sS][eE][nN][tT][aA][tT][iI][oO][nN]*
docs/*[rR][eE][sS][eE][aA][rR][cC][hH]*
docs/*.docx
docs/*.pptx
docs/*.pdf
scripts/*[pP][aA][pP][eE][rR]*


# local scratch
.commit-message.txt

# The paper source is code, not a deliverable binary: it must be versioned
# so the .docx can be rebuilt and audited.
!docs/build_research_paper.py
!docs/paper_content.py
!docs/verify_paper_docx.py

__pycache__/
